/* =====================================================================
   BIRCH PRACTICES . the growth plan library for young adults (GWG BLD 742)
   Built for young adults, 18 to 26.

   Same shapes as Pine's practices.js (and Sequoia's, and Oak's inline
   library), so an app built from Pine's app.js swaps PINE_PRACTICES for these:
     DOMAIN_DEFS  six parts: key, name, color, group, prompt, restore
                  [[name, line]], strength_msg, growth_steps
     GUIDES       "part|Name": {why, today, build, hard, vary?, adapt?}
                  for the restore practices
     G            the same, for the NEW practices
     META         part: {Name: [discipline, time, evidence, source url or '']}
     NEW          part: [[name, line]], appended to restore by the app
     EV, DISC     the same codes as Oak
     SRC          source urls used in META
     SHELF        part: [[title, url or '', line]] (Resource shelf)
     FLAGS        "part|Name": {strand: 'move' | 'rest' | 'nourish' (Leaves),
                  levels: ['gentle','moderate','athletic'], seated (has a
                  seated or low-energy way, in adapt), safety, faith (has a
                  Plain version in PLAIN), skills, season}
     SOURCES      "part|Name": source ids (shared/gg-sources.js) or
                  {label, href, adapted}, for PX 'birch:<practice>'
   Faith or Plain wording (decision 7, set by the person):
     PLAIN        "part|Name": {n, d, g} for every practice flagged faith.
                  n is the name shown in Plain wording (the stored key stays
                  "part|Name", so a person who switches keeps their practices),
                  d the one line, g the guide (vary is '' in Plain).
     PLAIN_PARTS  part: {prompt, strength_msg, growth_steps} where the Plain
                  wording differs (Roots only).
     PLAIN_SHELF  part: shelf list for Plain wording (Roots only).
   Extra for Birch:
     IDS          slug: "part|Name". A short stable id for every practice
                  (the name in lower case, spaces and marks turned to single
                  hyphens), so Groundwork's skills can say {practice: slug}.
                  The app also accepts the full "part|Name" key.
     SKILLS       "part|Name": [skill ids]. Practices that fit Skills I've Got
                  in Groundwork, by the skill ids in birch/groundwork.js SKILLS
                  (sk-resume, sk-budget, sk-cook, sk-doctor, and the rest).
                  A skill links to its practice through BY_SKILL. Also copied
                  into FLAGS[id].skills.
     BY_SKILL     tag: ["part|Name", ...], the same list turned around, so a
                  skill with no practice link can still offer a practice.
     SEASON       "part|Name": [season ids] from My Season (decision 6):
                  school, work, serve, parent, between. Practices tagged for
                  a person's season are shown first. Never changes scores.
                  Also copied into FLAGS[id].season.
   Adult faith rules (Oak's, never the kids' rules): faith is spoken about only
   where the practice is about faith; experience, never belief; questions and
   doubt are welcome; a faith community that hurt someone is met by listening.
   adapt (in a guide) is the seated or low-energy way of a movement practice.
   Edit words in the table below. No dashes; Title Case for practice names.
   No guides are linked yet (Birch's guides come next build).
   ===================================================================== */
